# Every text file is LF in the working tree, on every host, regardless of core.autocrlf.
#
# This project runs its scripts inside Linux containers from a bind mount of the working
# tree. On a Windows clone with autocrlf=true, git would check scripts/tf-check.sh out with
# CRLF endings, and busybox sh would then fail on the very first line with an error about
# an illegal option -- the "\r" is invisible in every editor and the message names nothing
# that exists. The same corruption would reach the Dockerfile, every YAML the cluster
# applies, and the Terraform the provider parses. One rule here removes the whole class.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary evidence artifacts must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.cast binary
